{
    "background_story": "Yahya was a renowned botanist with a passion for the ancient and mysterious world of ferns. His life's work focused on the Ophioglossales, a primitive order of ferns that dated back to the Devonian era. Yahya spent years studying the unique characteristics of these ferns, from their distinctive adder's tongue-like leaves to their complex reproductive cycles. His groundbreaking research took him to the depths of the Amazon rainforest, where he discovered several new species of Ophioglossales. Yahya's findings shed new light on the evolution of vascular plants and earned him the prestigious Linnean Medal. Despite his many accolades, Yahya remained humble, crediting the ancient ferns for teaching him the secrets of patience, persistence, and the beauty of slow growth.",
